      "created_at": "2026-08-03T17:22:20Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-03T17:22:20Z",
      "body": "**Correction to this PR's body.** It states the cover is \"induced by context-bundle geometry\" and that fixing the weak alignment \"would need an induction objective optimizing continuation discriminativeness.\" That is wrong — `induction.rs` already gates splits on next-token entropy reduction (`entropy_gain_bits`, default 0.25) and scores an information-bottleneck term including `I(Z;X) − β·I(Z;Y_future)`.\n\nThe corrected statement: candidate partitions come from geometry, and continuation structure only *vetoes* them — entropy gain is an acceptance filter, not the maximand. So the cover captures continuation structure only where it aligns with signature-space geometry. All measurements in this PR stand; the explanation of the cause does not. Full correction on #364.",
